<text layer="alpha" matrix="1 0 0 1 0 16" transformations="translations" pos="16 368" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="736" height="16.8964" depth="5.8164" valign="top">\textbf{Behauptung:} Für alle $n \in \mathbb N_0$ ist $n^3+2n$ durch 3 teilbar</text>
<text layer="beta" transformations="translations" pos="16 320" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="448" height="15.0516" depth="3.9738" valign="top">Zeigt die Behauptung mit vollständiger Induktion</text>
<text layer="gamma" matrix="1 0 0 1 0 16" transformations="translations" pos="16 320" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="512" height="13.078" depth="2.0202" valign="top">\bfseries Beweis</text>
<text layer="delta" matrix="1 0 0 1 0 16" transformations="translations" pos="16 288" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="608" height="16.8964" depth="5.8164" valign="top">I.A.: Es sei $n = 0$. Es gilt $0^3+2\cdot 0 = 0$</text>
<text layer="epsilon" matrix="1 0 0 1 0 16" transformations="translations" pos="16 256" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="608" height="13.946" depth="2.8638" valign="top">I.S.: $n-1 \rightsquigarrow n$</text>
<text matrix="1 0 0 1 16 16" transformations="translations" pos="16 224" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="576" height="15.6355" depth="4.551" valign="top" style="item">Sei $n\in \mathbb N_+$  fest aber beliebig</text>
<text layer="zeta" matrix="1 0 0 1 16 16" transformations="translations" pos="16 192" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="576" height="17.3893" depth="6.327" valign="top" style="item">I.V.: Es gelte $(n-1)^3 +2\cdot (n-1)$ ist durch 3 teilbar</text>
<text layer="eta" matrix="1 0 0 1 -16 32" transformations="translations" pos="48 176" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="720" height="104.482" depth="93.6174" valign="top">\begin{align*}
(n)^3 + 2\cdot (n) &amp;= (n \cdot n \cdot n) + 2 (( n - 1) + 1)\\
&amp;= ((n - 1) + 1)^3 + 2 (n - 1) + 2\\
&amp;=(n - 1)^3 + 3 (n - 1)^2 1 + 3 (n - 1) 1^2 + 1^3 + 2 (n - 1) + 2\\
&amp;= (n - 1)^3 + 2(n - 1) + 3 (n - 1)^2 + (n - 1) + 1 + 2 (n - 1) + 2\\
 \end{align*}</text>
<text layer="theta" matrix="1 0 0 1 16 -27" transformations="translations" pos="16 64" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="512" height="17.3893" depth="6.327" valign="top" style="item">Nach I.V. ist $(n - 1)^3 + 2 \cdot (n - 1)$ durch 3 teilbar</text>
<text matrix="1 0 0 1 16 -27" transformations="translations" pos="16 32" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="400" height="17.3893" depth="6.327" valign="top" style="item">$3(n - 1)^2 + 3(n-1) +3 $ ist durch 3 teilbar</text>
<text layer="iota" matrix="1 0 0 1 32 -48" transformations="translations" pos="432 48" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="192" height="14.4411" depth="3.3744" valign="top">$\Rightarrow \mathpzc A_{n}$ ist wahr</text>
<text layer="pagenumbers_page" matrix="1 0 0 1 13 6.058" transformations="translations" pos="-13 -35" stroke="black" type="label" width="11.7208" height="7.4796" depth="0.115" valign="top" size="veryTiny">{\bf 15}</text>
</page>
