<text transformations="translations" pos="16 368" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="576" height="13.229" depth="2.1534" valign="top">Sei $w$ ein Wort</text>
<text transformations="translations" pos="16 336" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="432" height="17.6912" depth="6.6156" valign="top">\textbf{Behauptung:} Für alle $k\in \mathbb N_0$ gilt $\vert w^k \vert = k\cdot \vert w \vert$</text>
<text layer="beta" matrix="1 0 0 1 0 -48" transformations="translations" pos="16 304" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="576" height="30.9335" depth="19.9134" valign="top">I.A.: Es sei $k = 0 $. Es gilt $\vert w ^k \vert = \vert w^0\vert = \vert \epsilon \vert = 0 = 0 \cdot \vert w\vert = k \cdot \vert w \vert $</text>
<text layer="gamma" matrix="1 0 0 1 0 -64" transformations="translations" pos="16 256" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="576" height="14.1392" depth="3.0636" valign="top">I.S.: $ k-1 \rightsquigarrow k$</text>
<text matrix="1 0 0 1 0 -64" transformations="translations" pos="16 224" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="576" height="15.671" depth="4.6176" valign="top" style="item">Sei $k \in \mathbb N_+$ beliebig</text>
<text layer="delta" matrix="1 0 0 1 0 -64" transformations="translations" pos="16 192" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="576" height="17.6912" depth="6.6156" valign="top" style="item">I.V.: Es gelte $\vert w^{k-1}\vert = (k-1)\cdot \vert w\vert$</text>
<text layer="epsilon" matrix="1 0 0 1 0 -48" transformations="translations" pos="16 144" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="576" height="20.7725" depth="9.7236" valign="top" style="item">$\vert w^{k} \vert =  \vert w^{k-1} \cdot w \vert  = \vert w^{k-1} \vert + \vert w \vert \stackrel{\text{I.V.}}{=}  (k-1) \cdot \vert w\vert + \vert w\vert  = k \cdot \vert w \vert$</text>
<text layer="alpha" transformations="translations" pos="16 288" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="576" height="13.078" depth="2.0202" valign="top">\bfseries Beweis</text>
<path layer="iota" matrix="1 0 0 1 61 -32" fill="white">
