</group>
<group matrix="1 0 0 1 16 0">
<path stroke="black" fill="KITblue15">
-8 184 m
512 184 l
8 0 0 -8 512 176 520 176 a
520 120.701 l
0 120.701 l
8 0 0 -8 0 128.701 -8 128.701 a
h
</path>
</group>
<text transformations="translations" pos="0 384" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="560" height="16.5901" depth="5.5278" valign="top" style="item">Sei nun $A = \{a,b\}$ ein Alphabet und</text>
<text matrix="1 0 0 1 0 5" transformations="translations" pos="32 320" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="208" height="44.198" depth="33.2112" valign="top">$$
x \mapsto \left\{ \begin{array}{ll}
xx &amp;\vert\; x=a \\
x &amp;\vert\; sonst
\end{array}\right.
$$</text>
<text matrix="1 0 0 1 -48 32" transformations="translations" pos="64 304" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="112" height="13.2268" depth="2.1312" valign="top">$f: A \rightarrow A^*$</text>
<text matrix="1 0 0 1 96 0" transformations="translations" pos="272 336" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="160" height="15.3757" depth="4.2846" valign="top">$g: A^* \rightarrow A^*$</text>
<text matrix="1 0 0 1 112 0" transformations="translations" pos="272 304" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="192" height="16.5901" depth="5.5278" valign="top">$g(\epsilon) = \epsilon$</text>
<text matrix="1 0 0 1 112 0" transformations="translations" pos="272 272" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="400" height="16.5901" depth="5.5278" valign="top">$g(xw) = f(x) \cdot g(w) \quad \quad x \in A, w\in A^*$</text>
<text matrix="1 0 0 1 0 -16" transformations="translations" pos="0 240" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="592" height="16.5901" depth="5.5278" valign="top" style="item">Außerdem sei $\vert w \vert_a$ die Anzahl der $a$&apos;s in w</text>
<text matrix="1 0 0 1 16 0" transformations="translations" pos="0 176" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="512" height="29.2241" depth="18.204" valign="top">Behauptung: Für alle $n\in \mathbb N_0$ gilt: für alle $w\in A^*$ der Länge $\vert w \vert = n$ gilt: $\vert g(w) \vert = 2\vert w \vert_a+ \vert w \vert_b$</text>
<text matrix="1 0 0 1 16 0" transformations="translations" pos="0 96" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="448" height="28.8067" depth="17.76" valign="top">Zeigt die Behauptung mit vollständiger Induktion über die Wortlänge $\vert w \vert = n$</text>
<text layer="pagenumbers_page" matrix="1 0 0 1 13 6.058" transformations="translations" pos="-13 -35" stroke="black" type="label" width="11.7208" height="7.4635" depth="0" valign="top" size="veryTiny">{\bf 17}</text>
</page>
<page title="Lösung">
<layer name="alpha"/>
<layer name="pagenumbers_page" edit="no"/>
<view layers="alpha pagenumbers_page" active="alpha"/>
<text layer="alpha" transformations="translations" pos="0 384" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="896" height="16.5901" depth="5.5278" valign="top">I.A.:  $n = 0 \Rightarrow \vert w \vert = 0 \Rightarrow w = \epsilon \Rightarrow \vert g(w)\vert =\vert g(\epsilon)\vert = \vert \epsilon\vert = 0 = 2\vert\epsilon\vert_a + \vert\epsilon\vert_b = 2\cdot 0 + 0$</text>
<text transformations="translations" pos="0 352" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="416" height="13.946" depth="2.8638" valign="top">I.S.: $n-1 \rightsquigarrow n$</text>
<text transformations="translations" pos="0 320" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="512" height="15.6355" depth="4.551" valign="top" style="item">Es sei $n \in \mathbb N_+$ beliebig</text>
<text transformations="translations" pos="0 288" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="768" height="16.5901" depth="5.5278" valign="top" style="item">I.V.: Für \textbf{alle} Wörter der Länge $\vert w\vert = n-1$ gilt $\vert g(w) \vert = 2\vert w \vert_a+ \vert w \vert_b$</text>
<text transformations="translations" pos="0 256" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="816" height="43.1146" depth="32.1234" valign="top" style="item">Es sei $w&apos;  \in A^*$ mit $\vert w&apos;\vert = n$ \\
Wir betrachten das erste Zeichen $x$ von $w&apos;$ ($w&apos; = x \cdot w )$\\
$\vert g(xw)\vert = \vert f(x) \vert  + \vert g(w)\vert$</text>
<text layer="pagenumbers_page" matrix="1 0 0 1 13 6.058" transformations="translations" pos="-13 -35" stroke="black" type="label" width="11.7208" height="7.4796" depth="0.115" valign="top" size="veryTiny">{\bf 18}</text>
</page>
<page title="Lösung">
<layer name="alpha"/>
<layer name="pagenumbers_page" edit="no"/>
<view layers="alpha pagenumbers_page" active="alpha"/>
<text layer="alpha" transformations="translations" pos="0 384" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="288" height="12.9115" depth="1.8204" valign="top">Fall 1: $x= a$</text>
<text transformations="translations" pos="0 352" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="672" height="16.6056" depth="5.55" valign="top" style="item">$\vert w&apos; \vert_a = \vert xw \vert_a = \vert w \vert_a+1,\quad \vert w&apos; \vert _b = \vert xw \vert_b = \vert w \vert_b$</text>
<text matrix="1 0 0 1 0 16" transformations="translations" pos="0 320" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="864" height="120.941" depth="110.156" valign="top">\begin{align*}
\vert g(w&apos;)\vert  = \vert g(xw)\vert &amp;= \vert f(x) \vert + \vert g(w)\vert \\
&amp;\stackrel{\text{I.V.}}{=} \vert aa\vert + 2 \vert w \vert_a+ \vert w \vert_b\\
&amp;= 2 + 2 \vert w \vert_a+ \vert w \vert_b\\
&amp;= 2 (1+\vert w \vert_a) + \vert w \vert_b\\
&amp;= 2 \vert xw \vert_a+ \vert xw \vert_b \quad \quad \text{wegen }\vert xw \vert_a= \vert w \vert_a+1, \vert xw \vert_b= \vert w \vert_b\\
&amp;= 2 \vert w&apos; \vert_a + \vert w&apos; \vert_b 
\end{align*}</text>
<text layer="pagenumbers_page" matrix="1 0 0 1 13 6.058" transformations="translations" pos="-13 -35" stroke="black" type="label" width="11.7208" height="7.4796" depth="0.115" valign="top" size="veryTiny">{\bf 19}</text>
</page>
<page title="Lösung">
<layer name="alpha"/>
<layer name="pagenumbers_page" edit="no"/>
<view layers="alpha pagenumbers_page" active="alpha"/>
<text layer="alpha" transformations="translations" pos="0 384" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="288" height="13.3289" depth="2.2644" valign="top">Fall 2: $x= b$</text>
<text transformations="translations" pos="0 352" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="736" height="16.6056" depth="5.55" valign="top" style="item">$\vert w&apos; \vert_a= \vert xw \vert_a= \vert w \vert_a, \quad \vert w&apos; \vert_b= \vert xw \vert_a= \vert w \vert_a+1 $</text>
<text matrix="1 0 0 1 0 16" transformations="translations" pos="0 320" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="416" height="104.393" depth="93.5286" valign="top">\begin{align*}
\vert g(w&apos;)\vert  = \vert g(xw)\vert &amp;= \vert f(x) \vert + \vert g(w)\vert \\
&amp;\stackrel{\text{I.V.}}{=} \vert b\vert + 2 \vert w \vert_a+ \vert w \vert_b\\
&amp;= 2 \vert w \vert_a + \vert w \vert_b +1 \\
&amp;= 2 \vert xw \vert_a + \vert xw \vert_b\\
&amp;= 2 \vert w&apos; \vert_a+ \vert w&apos; \vert_b
\end{align*}</text>
<text layer="pagenumbers_page" matrix="1 0 0 1 13 6.058" transformations="translations" pos="-13 -35" stroke="black" type="label" width="11.7208" height="7.4796" depth="0.115" valign="top" size="veryTiny">{\bf 20}</text>
</page>
<page title="Frühere Aussagen benutzen">
<layer name="alpha"/>
<layer name="beta"/>
<layer name="gamma"/>
<view layers="alpha" active="alpha"/>
<view layers="alpha beta" active="beta"/>
<group layer="beta">
<path stroke="black" fill="KITblue15">
8 312 m
864 312 l
8 0 0 -8 864 304 872 304 a
872 103.288 l
16 103.288 l
8 0 0 -8 16 111.288 8 111.288 a
h
</path>
</group>
<text layer="alpha" transformations="translations" pos="0 384" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="880" height="15.5977" depth="4.5288" valign="top" style="item">Bei Vollständiger Induktion benutzen wir oft nur $\mathpzc A_{n-1}$ um $\mathpzc A_{n}$ zu beweisen</text>
<text transformations="translations" pos="0 352" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="720" height="15.5977" depth="4.5288" valign="top" style="item">Manchmal ist es einfacher auch die Aussagen $\mathpzc A_0$ bis $\mathpzc A_{n-1}$ zu benutzen</text>
<text layer="beta" matrix="1 0 0 1 16 0" transformations="translations" pos="0 304" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="368" height="15.0605" depth="3.996" valign="top">\bfseries Beispiel</text>
<text matrix="1 0 0 1 16 0" transformations="translations" pos="0 272" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="848" height="15.4334" depth="4.3512" valign="top">Jede Zahl $\in\mathbb N_0$ kann als Summe paarweise verschiedener Zweierpotenzen dargestellt werden</text>
<text matrix="1 0 0 1 16 0" transformations="translations" pos="0 240" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="800" height="15.2758" depth="4.218" valign="top">$\mathpzc A_n: n$ kann als Summe paarweise verschiedener Zweierpotenzen dargestellt werden</text>
<text matrix="1 0 0 1 144 0" transformations="translations" pos="0 208" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="528" height="54.3345" depth="43.3788" valign="top">Wir suchen also eine Menge Z von Zweierpotenzen, sodass $$n = \sum_{z\in Z} \limits z$$</text>
<text layer="gamma" transformations="translations" pos="0 96" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="864" height="26.4002" depth="15.3402" valign="top" style="item">Man kann auch mehrere Induktionsanfänge machen, z.B. wenn sich gerade/ungerade Zahlen verschieden verhalten</text>
</page>
<page title="Beispiel">
<layer name="alpha"/>
<layer name="beta"/>
<layer name="gamma"/>
<layer name="delta"/>
<layer name="epsilon"/>
<layer name="zeta"/>
<layer name="eta"/>
<layer name="theta"/>
<view layers="alpha" active="alpha"/>
<view layers="alpha beta" active="beta"/>
<view layers="alpha beta gamma" active="gamma"/>
<view layers="alpha beta gamma delta" active="delta"/>
<view layers="alpha beta gamma delta epsilon" active="epsilon"/>
<view layers="alpha beta gamma delta epsilon zeta" active="zeta"/>
<view layers="alpha beta gamma delta epsilon zeta eta" active="eta"/>
<view layers="alpha beta gamma delta epsilon zeta eta theta" active="theta"/>
<group layer="theta" matrix="0.974138 0 0 1 -0.206897 0">
<path stroke="black" fill="KITgreen15">
-8 392 m
912 392 l
8 0 0 -8 912 384 920 384 a
920 4.21536 l
0 4.21536 l
8 0 0 -8 0 12.2154 -8 12.2154 a
h
</path>
</group>
<text layer="alpha" transformations="translations" pos="0 384" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="384" height="13.0048" depth="1.9092" valign="top">\textbf{I.A.:} n = 0</text>
<text transformations="translations" pos="0 352" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="512" height="16.5901" depth="5.5278" valign="top">Die leere Summe hat den Wert 0 ($Z = \{\}$)</text>
<text layer="beta" transformations="translations" pos="0 320" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="448" height="15.4334" depth="4.3512" valign="top">\textbf{I.S.:}  $n-1 \rightsquigarrow  n$ Sei $n \in \mathbb N_0$ fest aber beliebig.</text>
<text layer="gamma" matrix="1 0 0 1 16 -54" transformations="translations" pos="0 288" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="896" height="17.6423" depth="6.5712" valign="top">Wähle $i = \max \{j \in \mathbb N_0  \vert 2^j \leq n\} $. Dann lässt sich n schreiben als $n = 2^i  + m$ mit $m \in \mathbb N_0 , m &lt; n$</text>
<text layer="delta" matrix="1 0 0 1 16 -54" transformations="translations" pos="0 256" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="896" height="17.0185" depth="5.9496" valign="top">Außerdem $m &lt; 2^i$ da sonst $n \ge 2^i + 2^i = 2^{i+1}$ Widerspruch zu $i = \max \dots$</text>
<text layer="epsilon" matrix="1 0 0 1 16 -54" transformations="translations" pos="0 224" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="896" height="17.6423" depth="6.5712" valign="top">Falls $m = 0$ ist Z einfach $\{2^i\}$ und wir sind fertig.</text>
<text layer="zeta" matrix="1 0 0 1 16 -56" transformations="translations" pos="0 192" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="880" height="30.9912" depth="19.98" valign="top">Falls nicht, können wir die $\underset{\text{Starke Induktion } m \text{ evtl } \neq n-1}{\underbrace{\text{I.V. auf } m \text { anwenden}}}$. D.h. es gibt eine Menge $Z&apos;$, sodass $\sum_{z\in Z&apos;} \limits z = m $</text>
<text layer="eta" matrix="1 0 0 1 16 -54" transformations="translations" pos="0 128" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="896" height="17.6423" depth="6.5712" valign="top">Da $2^i \not \in Z&apos;$ ($m &lt; 2^i$) finden wir $Z = Z&apos; \cup \{2^i\}$</text>
<text layer="beta" transformations="translations" pos="16 288" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="688" height="28.7335" depth="17.6934" valign="top">\textbf{I.V.:} Für alle $k \in \mathbb N_0$  mit $k &lt; n$ gilt: $k$ kann als Summe paarweiser verschiedener Zweierpotenzen dargestellt werden</text>
<text layer="theta" transformations="translations" pos="16 32" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="880" height="15.4334" depth="4.3512" valign="top">$\Rightarrow$ die Aussage gilt für alle $n\in \mathbb N_0$</text>
</page>
</ipe>
